cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "qopt: a verified Clifford+T circuit optimizer for T and CNOT counts"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - given-names: Maksym
    family-names: Shchehlov
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum circuit optimization
  - Clifford+T
  - T-count
  - CNOT count
  - logical AND
  - measurement-based uncomputation
  - verification
abstract: >-
  qopt reduces the T count and the CNOT count of Clifford+T circuits given as Toffoli networks.
  It provides a unitary mode (portfolio of evolved rewriting programs, phase folding, optional neural block
  resynthesis) and measurement-based modes that place Gidney logical-AND gates with measurement-based
  uncomputation automatically by tracking every wire as a polynomial over GF(2). Every reported circuit is
  re-checked by an independent state-vector simulator (up to 22 qubits) or a sum-over-paths checker.
repository-code: "https://github.com/seglovmaksim695-creator/qopt"
url: "https://github.com/seglovmaksim695-creator/qopt"
